<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="utf-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
    <title>Miga | Tiny Neighborhood Sourdough Bakery</title>
    <meta name="description" content="Miga is a one-baker neighborhood sourdough bakery with weekly small-batch loaves, long fermentation, and Sunday morning pickup windows.">
    <meta property="og:title" content="Miga | Tiny Neighborhood Sourdough Bakery">
    <meta property="og:description" content="Warm, slow-fermented sourdough from one baker to the neighborhood.">
    <meta property="og:image" content="assets/hero.jpg">
    <meta property="og:type" content="website">
    <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com">
    <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.gstatic.com" crossorigin>
    <link href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Fraunces:opsz,wght@9..144,500..800&family=Source+Sans+3:wght@400;600;700;800&display=swap" rel="stylesheet">
    <link rel="preload" as="image" href="assets/hero.jpg" fetchpriority="high">
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="styles.css">
  </head>
  <body>
    <header class="site-header" aria-label="Main navigation">
      <a class="brand" href="#top" aria-label="Miga home">
        <span class="brand-mark">m</span>
        <span>Miga</span>
      </a>
      <nav>
        <a href="#process">Process</a>
        <a href="#bakes">Bakes</a>
        <a href="#pickup">Pickup</a>
      </nav>
    </header>

    <main id="top">
      <section class="hero">
        <div class="hero-copy reveal">
          <p class="eyebrow">one baker · neighborhood pickup · naturally leavened</p>
          <h1>Miga</h1>
          <p class="hero-lede">Slow sourdough for the kind of morning that asks for a torn heel of bread, salted butter, and nothing hurried.</p>
          <div class="hero-actions" aria-label="Primary actions">
            <a class="button primary" href="#pickup">Reserve this week</a>
            <a class="button ghost" href="#bakes">See the bake list</a>
          </div>
        </div>
        <figure class="hero-photo reveal" style="--delay: 120ms">
          <img src="assets/hero.jpg" width="1280" height="1600" alt="Fresh sourdough loaves resting on brown paper in warm light" fetchpriority="high" decoding="sync">
          <figcaption>Long-fermented loaves baked in small morning runs.</figcaption>
        </figure>
        <aside class="hero-note reveal" style="--delay: 220ms" aria-label="This week at Miga">
          <span class="note-kicker">This Sunday</span>
          <strong>12 country loaves</strong>
          <span>Pickup 9:30-11:00 · starter fed Friday night</span>
        </aside>
      </section>

      <section class="counter-strip" aria-label="Sensory notes">
        <span>crackly crust</span>
        <span>custardy crumb</span>
        <span>mild tang</span>
        <span>toasted sesame</span>
        <span>olive oil shine</span>
      </section>

      <section class="process section" id="process">
        <div class="section-heading reveal">
          <p class="eyebrow">from flour to crumb</p>
          <h2>The loaf keeps its own slow clock.</h2>
          <p>Each bake starts before the weekend does: starter refreshed, dough folded by hand, baskets tucked under linen, and the oven brought up until the crust can blister.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="process-grid">
          <article class="step reveal">
            <img src="assets/flour-bowl.jpg" width="1067" height="1600" alt="Flour falling into a glass bowl">
            <div>
              <span>01 · flour</span>
              <h3>Fresh-milled mood, simple pantry.</h3>
              <p>Bread flour, whole grain, water, salt, and a starter that gets more attention than most houseplants.</p>
            </div>
          </article>
          <article class="step wide reveal" style="--delay: 80ms">
            <img src="assets/dough-hands.jpg" width="1600" height="1067" alt="Hands folding sourdough on a floured workbench">
            <div>
              <span>02 · fold</span>
              <h3>Strength built quietly.</h3>
              <p>Coil folds, rest, and another patient turn until the dough feels airy and alive.</p>
            </div>
          </article>
          <article class="step reveal" style="--delay: 120ms">
            <img src="assets/rest-proofing-linen.jpg" width="1125" height="750" alt="Sourdough dough proofing between folded linen cloths">
            <div>
              <span>03 · rest</span>
              <h3>Tucked in until ready.</h3>
              <p>Baskets stay covered while the dough proofs slowly and keeps its own soft schedule.</p>
            </div>
          </article>
          <article class="step reveal">
            <img src="assets/prebake-scoring-lame.jpg" width="1071" height="750" alt="Hands scoring flour-dusted unbaked bread dough with a lame">
            <div>
              <span>04 · score</span>
              <h3>A quick blade before heat.</h3>
              <p>The slash tells the loaf where to open, then steam and stone do the rest.</p>
            </div>
          </article>
          <article class="step wide reveal" style="--delay: 80ms">
            <img src="assets/hands-loaf.jpg" width="1068" height="1600" alt="Hands holding a fresh baked loaf">
            <div>
              <span>05 · bake</span>
              <h3>Hot enough to sing.</h3>
              <p>The oven gives the crust its crackle, the loaf comes out fragrant, and the room goes quiet for a minute.</p>
            </div>
          </article>
          <article class="step reveal" style="--delay: 160ms">
            <img src="assets/open-crumb.jpg" width="1600" height="1036" alt="Close view of open sourdough crumb">
            <div>
              <span>06 · crumb</span>
              <h3>Soft chew, clean tang.</h3>
              <p>Made for butter melting into the holes, soup at the edge of the bowl, or a first slice over the sink.</p>
            </div>
          </article>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="menu section" id="bakes">
        <div class="menu-board reveal">
          <div class="board-top">
            <p class="eyebrow">weekly bake list</p>
            <p class="chalk-date">Aug 8-9</p>
          </div>
          <h2>Small batches, posted every Wednesday.</h2>
          <div class="bake-list" aria-label="Miga weekly menu">
            <article class="bake-item">
              <div>
                <h3>Country loaf</h3>
                <p>White, whole wheat, rye · blistered crust · mild tang</p>
              </div>
              <strong>$12</strong>
            </article>
            <article class="bake-item">
              <div>
                <h3>Sesame batard</h3>
                <p>Toasted sesame, tender chew, nutty finish</p>
              </div>
              <strong>$14</strong>
            </article>
            <article class="bake-item">
              <div>
                <h3>Olive & herb</h3>
                <p>Castelvetrano olives, rosemary, olive oil gloss</p>
              </div>
              <strong>$15</strong>
            </article>
            <article class="bake-item">
              <div>
                <h3>Morning focaccia</h3>
                <p>Soft squares, flaky salt, garlic oil, pickup warm</p>
              </div>
              <strong>$6</strong>
            </article>
          </div>
          <p class="board-note">Preorders close Friday at noon or when the bench is full.</p>
        </div>
        <figure class="menu-photo reveal" style="--delay: 120ms">
          <img src="assets/morning-counter.jpg" width="1600" height="1197" alt="A morning table set with bread and milk">
          <figcaption>Pickup is a porch table, a paper bag, and bread still talking as it cools.</figcaption>
        </figure>
      </section>

      <section class="story section">
        <figure class="story-photo reveal">
          <img src="assets/hands-loaf.jpg" width="1068" height="1600" alt="Hands holding a fresh baked loaf">
        </figure>
        <div class="story-copy reveal" style="--delay: 100ms">
          <p class="eyebrow">the one-baker rhythm</p>
          <h2>Hi, I’m Mina. Miga is the crumb I bring to the block.</h2>
          <p>I bake from a home oven with a deck-bake obsession: small enough to know every loaf, steady enough that neighbors can plan breakfast around it.</p>
          <p>The starter lives on the counter, gets fed twice before a bake, and decides the schedule with the weather. If the dough needs another hour, it gets another hour.</p>
          <dl class="proof-list">
            <div>
              <dt>Fermentation</dt>
              <dd>18-24 hours for flavor, chew, and easier slicing.</dd>
            </div>
            <div>
              <dt>Batch size</dt>
              <dd>Usually 12-18 loaves, shaped by hand.</dd>
            </div>
            <div>
              <dt>Pickup</dt>
              <dd>Sunday mornings while the bags are still warm.</dd>
            </div>
          </dl>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="crumb-section section" aria-label="Crumb detail">
        <div class="crumb-copy reveal">
          <p class="eyebrow">miga means crumb</p>
          <h2>The inside is the promise.</h2>
          <p>Open but not empty, glossy but not gummy, with enough structure for a thick swipe of butter.</p>
        </div>
        <figure class="crumb-photo reveal" style="--delay: 100ms">
          <img src="assets/crumb-hands.jpg" width="1060" height="1600" alt="Hands holding a torn piece of bread showing its crumb">
        </figure>
      </section>

      <section class="pickup section" id="pickup">
        <div class="pickup-panel reveal">
          <p class="eyebrow">preorder rhythm</p>
          <h2>Send a note, choose a loaf, pick up on Sunday.</h2>
          <p>Text your order by Friday noon. I’ll confirm the bake, tuck your name on a bag, and have it waiting between 9:30 and 11:00 Sunday morning.</p>
          <a class="button primary" href="mailto:hello@migabakery.example?subject=Sunday%20Miga%20preorder">hello@migabakery.example</a>
        </div>
        <div class="pickup-card reveal" style="--delay: 120ms">
          <span class="note-kicker">How to keep it happy</span>
          <ul>
            <li>Leave the cut side down on a board for day one.</li>
            <li>Bag it in linen or paper once fully cool.</li>
            <li>Toast slices from frozen for midweek butter emergencies.</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </section>
    </main>

    <footer>
      <p>Miga · Tiny neighborhood sourdough</p>
      <div class="footer-links">
        <a href="CREDITS.md">Photo credits</a>
        <a href="#top">Back to the counter</a>
      </div>
    </footer>

    <script src="script.js"></script>
  </body>
</html>
